  derived from: so101.urdf (same directory) - links, joints, limits, inertials, and mesh
  references translated mechanically; URDF joint <origin> becomes the SDF joint <pose
  relative_to="parent_link">, each child link pose is relative_to its parent joint frame,
  and joint axes stay in the joint frame (SDF >= 1.7 default), matching URDF axis semantics
  units: meters, kilograms, radians | meshes: meshes/*.stl authored in meters (no scale)
  materials: URDF colors mapped to per-visual diffuse/ambient (3d_printed 1.0 0.82 0.12;
  sts3215 0.1 0.1 0.1)
  omitted vs URDF: <transmission> blocks (ros_control config, not SDFormat)
  assumptions:
  - inertials copied unchanged from the URDF (original source: SO-ARM100/so101 CAD export)
  - gripper_frame_link keeps its near-zero placeholder inertial from the URDF
  - collision geometry reuses the visual meshes, matching the upstream URDF; the bundled
    validator warns about this - simplify collisions before heavy physics use
-->
